# Asker two-host deploy — Mac (M5 Max) env template.
#
# On the Mac: copy this to deploy/compose/.env (gitignored, auto-loaded by
# compose), then run `make mac-up`. The Mac runs only the async indexing
# workers (ingest + enrich); the browser just points at http://${PC_HOST}:13001.
# See docs/two-host-deploy.md.

# === REQUIRED ================================================================
# The PC's STATIC LAN IP — MUST be identical to PC_HOST in the PC's .env (it is
# the address the PC's Redpanda advertises and where TEI/CLIP/Redis are
# published). Do NOT use a *.local (Bonjour/mDNS) name: these workers run inside
# Docker Desktop's Linux VM, which does not resolve macOS mDNS, so a .local
# value never connects. Example: 192.168.1.50
PC_HOST=192.168.1.50

# === Worker fan-out ==========================================================
# How many of each async worker to run. Effective parallelism per consumer group
# is capped by the consumed topic's Kafka PARTITION COUNT — which is 4 by default
# (ADR-004) for docs.raw/docs.chunked — AND is shared with the PC's OWN ingest/
# enrich (same groups). So total active consumers per group = min(4, PC(1) + Mac
# replicas); extras idle. The default 2 here keeps you within the cap. The
# partition count is NOT env-configurable and existing topics are not reconciled;
# to go higher, manually add partitions on the PC (`rpk topic add-partitions
# docs.chunked -n N`). See docs/two-host-deploy.md.
INGEST_REPLICAS=2
ENRICH_REPLICAS=2

# === Models (MUST match the PC's TEI/CLIP and the deployed Vespa schema) ======
EMBEDDING_DIM=1024
CLIP_DIM=512
